  "description": "Make tender, flaky salmon in under 30 minutes with this foolproof low-and-slow recipe, served with a bright, caper-packed tartar sauce.",
  "notes": "Notes: A 1.36 to 1.81 kg side of salmon can be used in place of fish fillets if desired. The fish will need to cook for an additional 5 to 10 minutes. Use an instant-read thermometer and insert it into the thickest part of the fish to determine doneness.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The tartar sauce can be made up to 3 days in advance and refrigerated in an airtight container. Leftover salmon can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 3 days. Reheat, wrapped in aluminum foil, at 135°C until warmed through.",
